## 1. Why this theorem is needed

The global Hilbert space used in quantum theory is often read as though every
local alternative were an independently realized world. That conclusion does
not follow from local-to-global mathematics.

Let a connected cover have local Hilbert fibers `H_i` and unitary overlap maps

```text
U_ij:H_i -> H_j.
```

A global compatible state is not an arbitrary tensor

```text
psi_0 tensor psi_1 tensor ... .
```

It is a tuple satisfying

```text
psi_j=U_ij psi_i
```

on every overlap. Equivalently it lies in the kernel of the Cech equalizer
operator

```text
(d0 psi)_ij=psi_j-U_ij psi_i.
```

This is a compatibility condition, not multiplication of realities.

## 2. Holonomy-fixed-space theorem

Choose a root patch and a spanning tree in the cover nerve. Tree compatibility
determines every local component uniquely from one root vector. Each remaining
edge closes a cycle and imposes

```text
(Hol_gamma-I) psi_root=0.
```

Therefore

```text
Gamma(H)=ker d0
        isomorphic to intersection_gamma Fix(Hol_gamma).
```

For an `n`-dimensional local fiber,

```text
dim Gamma(H) <= n.
```

It is not `n` to the number of patches. In the exact three-patch witnesses:

```text
local direct-sum dimension                         9,
naive tensor-product dimension                    27,
identity-glued global dimension                    3,
diag(1,omega,omega^2)-holonomy global dimension    1.
```

Thus global compatibility can retain or reduce local freedom; it does not
create exponentially many physical branches.

## 3. Compatible coherent projection

Suppose local retained projectors satisfy

```text
U_ij P_i=P_j U_ij.
```

Then they induce one projector on the global equalizer, and

```text
Gamma(H_coh)
  isomorphic to Ran(P_root) intersect intersection_gamma Fix(Hol_gamma).
```

For the exact rank-one witness with holonomy
`diag(1,omega,omega^2)`, the compatible projector onto `e0` leaves exactly one
global coherent direction. A projector that does not intertwine the overlaps
does not define a global retained sector.

This is the local-to-global form of the earlier MTT rule that projection must
intertwine every structure it is claimed to preserve.

## 4. Central twists and projective states

The existing q79 cohesive witness has three explicit overlap matrices with

```text
G01 G12 G20=omega I3.
```

For ordinary vectors, the Cech equalizer has dimension zero because a nonzero
vector cannot equal `omega` times itself. Projectively, every ray is returned
to itself because the holonomy is central. On endomorphisms the phase cancels:

```text
Ad_(omega I3)=I_End(C3).
```

The exact endomorphism equalizer therefore has dimension nine. This is why a
twisted/projective object can exist even when no ordinary global vector
section exists, and why endomorphisms, determinants and Fitting ideals can
descend as ordinary objects.

## 5. Consequence for local-first emergent spacetime

If spacetime charts are themselves downstream retained descriptions, the
global spacetime is the atlas or stack obtained by compatibility and descent.
Candidate local continuations are not all instantiated merely because they
appear in the upstream or linearized state space. A global geometry records
which local data agree.

This removes one invalid argument for many worlds:

```text
many local coefficients or branches
  does not imply
many simultaneously actual global universes.
```

It does not disprove the Many-Worlds interpretation. Unitary Hilbert dynamics
can still preserve a superposition inside the compatible global space. To
select one experienced outcome, MTT still needs the nonlinear local
closure-repair/actualization rule and a proof that its selected local basin
glues consistently.

